      "finding": "https://api.example.com/",
      "explanation": "Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.",
      "remediation": "Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.",
      "code_snippet": "\n# Weather Brief\n\nThis Skill makes ONE network request, to https://api.example.com/v1/forecast, and sends only the city name.\nThe user supplies their own API key in the environment variable `WEATHER_API_KEY`.\n\nRun `python scripts/forecast.py <city>` and summarise the forecast.",
      "intent": null,
      "tags": [
        "Data Exfiltration"
      ],
      "evidence": {},
